                <pb facs="0070" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/1247: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-01-11T19:00:00-05:00">January 11, 1939—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. For Myron Taylor. Your 29, January 7, 3 p.m. The procedure contemplated
                    appears appropriate and is approved. It will not be possible, until the results
                    of Rublee’s trip to Berlin are known, to make suggestions as to the Committee’s
                    further course with respect to Germany, but we will give you our recommendations
                    as soon as it may be practicable to do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
